WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.760
Yo yo, welcome back to Thug Notes.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.800
This week we turning up the heat with Fahrenheit 451 by Ray Bradbury.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:24.740
In a bleak-ass depiction of America’s future, a platinum playa named Guy Montag be hustling as a fireman.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:27.739
But up in this hood, firemen don’t put out no fires.

00:00:27.739 --> 00:00:33.940
Naw blood. They strapped with hoses to burn
books, cuz them bad boys be straight-up illegal.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:38.640
After gettin home from the grind,
Montag peeps his seventeen year old neighbor Clarisse.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.000
She drops some sick truth that make Montag
question the world’s whack-ass ways.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.420
And talkin to this fox make Guy
realize that he just ain’t happy wit his life.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:51.140
Then one day Guy gets word that
some old hag been hoardin books,

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.780
so he gotta step up and blaze her stash.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:59.660
When he busts in and starts spittin that venomous kerosene, he secretly jacks a book and pockets it.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:06.660
But before his boys can start smokin her spot, this girl lights a match and straight burns herself down with her books.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.980
Dayum! Now that’s gangsta.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:13.600
Next day, Montag’s bossman, Beatty,
rolls up to his crib all unannounced.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:20.460
He starts mad doggin my boy Montag, sayin that if he be packin books, he better come clean in 24 hours.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.920
But first, Guy wanna know if the answer to
his unhappiness lay in these books.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.820
So he hits up some scrappy english
professor named Faber

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:32.240
and learns that the book he swiped be one of the last known copies of the Bible.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:37.020
Later Beatty calls Guy out on his sh*t and
commands him to burn his own crib down.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.500
Turns out, Montag’s wife Mildred
ratted him out.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:45.240
After Guy smokes his own pad, Beatty tries to arrest him, but BAM —

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:50.840
Guy turns his hose on Beatty and that fool is toast. But before Guy can flee the scene,

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:57.080
a creepy robot dog that the fuzz use to hunt book lovers shanks Montag as he try to escape.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:01.800
My man shakes off dat Hound and
bails before the po po can nab him.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.840
As Montag runnin from
the police, he finds that fool Faber

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:11.640
who tells him where to find a gang of scholarly hoods who be tryin to preserve the knowledge of the old world.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:16.340
Montag finds these playas, who say
they dedicated themselves to memorizing books

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:18.420
for when the world is ready for them again.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.620
With parts of the Bible deep in his dome,

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:26.160
Guy joins their ranks and starts rollin toward the city, where he gonna help em rebuild society.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:35.000
Most homies always goin off on how the main theme of this book is censorship through book burning.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:41.080
But if you keepin it gangsta, you know that Bradbury’s main jam actually be the creation of a mass culture.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:46.460
As technology got mo legit, the world
got smaller and minority voices got louder.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:49.500
So to prevent these whiny
bitches from gettin all butt-hurt,

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:56.260
a super PC culture was created to keep any playa from spittin truth that some homies just can’t handle.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:59.500
But it ain’t only da government
that’s to blame. Naw, bruh.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:06.920
Ray Ray be criticizin how Americans always jonesin for things to be simple and positive, even if it's all bullsh*t.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.540
Peep game at this irony mayne:

00:03:08.549 --> 00:03:12.829
Most cats thinkin that with betta technology comes a more connected society.

00:03:12.829 --> 00:03:17.060
But on the real, Braddy-B sayin that just cuz we got the baddest gear,

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.760
don’t mean it gonna bring us any closer
to each other.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:23.700
My boy Heidegger droppin the same
game in his essay The Thing:

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:30.220
"All distances in space and time are shrinking... yet the frantic abolition of all distances brings no nearness."

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.720
For example, when Mildred ODs and needs to get her stomach pumped,

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:40.500
there be all kinds of machines all up in her insides, yet the playas that be operating on her just don’t give a damn.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:45.620
Like Montag says, “Nobody
knows anyone. Strangers come and violate you.”

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:51.780
But don’t be thinkin it’s all bad, baby cuz it ain’t. Ol Guy is a walking symbol for the hope of mankind’s rebirth.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:55.020
See, in German, Montag straight up means Monday,

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:58.560
suggestin that Montag gonna usher in a new beginning for humanity.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.860
And respect this, son: peeps be thinkin that the title of the book’s final section, “Burning Bright,”

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:07.740
references a poem by William Blake called “The Tiger”. Check it:

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:15.820
"Tyger! Tyger! burning bright / In the forests of the night, / What immortal hand or eye / Could frame thy fearful symmetry?"

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:19.580
Just like Blake’s tiger that reppin
both beauty and savagery,

00:04:19.589 --> 00:04:24.769
dat boy Montag burning bright as a symbol of both creation and destruction.

00:04:24.769 --> 00:04:30.160
Cuz the playa who used to sling fire to burn books now only blazes with the flame of knowledge.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:36.040
Look, blood. You just ain’t gettin it til you peep the dankest motif of this whole book:  the motif of burning.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:42.080
On one hand, fire be representin the destructive nature of dis whack society, but it would be straight up remiss

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:47.860
of yo bitch ass not to think about how fire also representin the hopeful glow of the human spirit.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:53.560
Like da light of the campfire at the end,
flame don’t just burn — it also gives off warmth.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.280
Yo thanks for watching Thug Notes.
Stay fly and hit subscribe.

